CellLabel

Copyright (c) 2026 Max Buckwalter-Chiang. All rights reserved.

This licence covers the CellLabel application. It does not cover the TrueTH
model file, which has its own licence. See section 4.


1. Free for research

You may install and use CellLabel free of charge for academic research,
teaching and private study. Research funded by a government body, a
university or a non-profit foundation counts as academic research. You may
install it on as many machines as you need and pass copies to colleagues at
your institution.

You may publish results produced with CellLabel without restriction, and
without asking. Please cite it (see CITATION.cff).


2. Commercial use needs a separate licence

You need a separate licence to use CellLabel in a business. This includes
paid contract or service work, and research done by or for a company. To
ask for one, open an issue at
https://github.com/mbc210/celllabel-releases/issues

You need written permission to sell, rent or sublicense CellLabel. You also
need it to take CellLabel apart to build a competing product.


3. Your data

CellLabel works on your own computer. It does not send your images or
counts anywhere. This licence gives nobody any rights over them.


4. The TrueTH model file is not covered by this licence

CellLabel ships with models/trueth/trueth.onnx, the TrueTH network converted
to ONNX. That file comes from the TrueTH project and is licensed under the
GNU General Public License, version 3.

Sections 1 and 2 above do not apply to it. You may use, copy, modify and
redistribute that file under the terms of the GPL, and nothing in this
licence restricts or adds conditions to those terms. The full GPL text ships
beside the file as models/trueth/LICENSE. The original TrueTH weights and
the script that converted them are listed in models/trueth/README.md. The
GPL calls these the corresponding source.

If you delete that file, CellLabel still works. Only the TrueTH option in
Detect goes away.


5. No warranty

CellLabel is provided as is, with no warranty of any kind, express or
implied. It is a research tool, not a medical device, and must not be used
to inform diagnosis or treatment. Check the counts it produces yourself.
To the extent the law allows, the author is not liable for any claim,
damage or loss arising from its use.
